: "libfwupdplugin/fu-coswid-firmware.c", "function": "fu_coswid_firmware_parse_entity", "line": 430, "var": "tag_id", "code": "tag_id = cbor_get_uint8(pairs[i].key);", "note": "Reads the tag ID from each entity map key; attacker controls these keys."}, {"step": 13, "file": "libfwupdplugin/fu-coswid-firmware.c", "function": "fu_coswid_firmware_parse_entity", "line": 440, "var": "pairs[i].value", "code": "if (tag_id == FU_COSWID_TAG_ROLE) { if (cbor_isa_uint(pairs[i].value)) { FuCoswidEntityRole role = cbor_get_uint8(pairs[i].value); entity->roles[entity_role_cnt++] = role; } }", "note": "When the ROLE tag (33) is encountered and the value is a uint, the role is written to entity->roles[entity_role_cnt++] WITHOUT a bounds check on entity_role_cnt; the roles array has only 6 elements (G_N_ELEMENTS(entity->roles) == 6)."}, {"step": 14, "file": "libfwupdplugin/fu-coswid-firmware.c", "function": "fu_coswid_firmware_parse_entity", "line": 445, "var": "entity->roles[entity_role_cnt]", "code": "entity->roles[entity_role_cnt++] = role;", "note": "With 6 or more uint ROLE values in the entity map, entity_role_cnt exceeds 5 and the write goes past the 6-element roles array, causing a heap-buffer-overflow WRITE past the FuCoswidFirmwareEntity allocation."}, {"step": 15, "file": "libfwupdplugin/fu-coswid-firmware.c", "function": "fu_coswid_firmware_parse_entity", "line": 450, "var": "value", "code": "for (guint j = 0; j < cbor_array_size(pairs[i].value); j++) { g_autoptr(cbor_item_t) value = cbor_array_get(pairs[i].value, j); FuCoswidEntityRole role = cbor_get_uint8(value); }", "note": "If pairs[i].value is an array, each element is read with cbor_get_uint8 without type checking; if an element is not a uint, libcbor reads item->data as an integer, which for non-uint types is a pointer into heap memory, leading to a heap-buffer-overflow READ 4 when the pointer value is dereferenced or interpreted as a 4-byte integer."}, {"step": 16, "file": "libfwupdplugin/fu-coswid-firmware.c", "